WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.756
Oracle Cloud Infrastructure matters here

2
00:00:02.756 --> 00:00:05.537
because the HR platform
runs on Oracle Cloud.

3
00:00:05.537 --> 00:00:14.412
Every VCN gets a dedicated resolver,
listening on 169.254.169.254.

4
00:00:14.412 --> 00:00:18.189
It answers from the private
views attached to it, in order,

5
00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:22.449
then its default view, then its
resolver rules, then the internet.

6
00:00:22.449 --> 00:00:25.057
Oracle says it performs recursion to the

7
00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:28.200
internet and DNSSEC
validation for signed zones.

8
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.787
The trap is in that order.

9
00:00:29.787 --> 00:00:33.650
A match in the sequence ends
resolution, even an NXDOMAIN.

10
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.721
So a private zone for
example dot com hides a

11
00:00:36.721 --> 00:00:40.048
forwarding rule for onprem
dot example dot com.

12
00:00:40.048 --> 00:00:42.863
Views can be attached to many resolvers,

13
00:00:42.863 --> 00:00:46.275
sharing private DNS data
across VCNs in a region.

14
00:00:46.275 --> 00:00:50.812
Same-name private and public
zones give split-horizon DNS.

15
00:00:50.812 --> 00:00:56.180
Between VCNs, resolution uses resolver
endpoints over a peering gateway.
